Kano Connect - Render Deployment Environment Variables
=====================================================

This document lists all environment variables required for the Kano Connect application
deployed on Render, along with the APIs and services used in the project.

--- PROJECT OVERVIEW ---
Kano Connect is an enterprise logistics/delivery platform with multi-role dashboards
(Customer, Rider, Dispatcher, Admin, Super Admin), live GPS tracking over Socket.IO,
Paystack payments, Cloudinary uploads, Nodemailer emails, Recharts reports, and a PWA.

--- API SERVICES AND INTEGRATIONS ---

1. MONGODB (Database)
   - Service: MongoDB
   - Used for: User data, shipments, deliveries, orders, ratings
   - Connection: MONGODB_URI environment variable
   - Documentation: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/

2. PAYSTACK (Payments)
   - Service: Paystack (Africa payment gateway)
   - Used for: Payment processing, transaction validation, refunds
   - Keys needed:
     * PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY - Server-side secret key
     * PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY - Frontend public key
   - Documentation: https://paystack.com/docs
   - API endpoints:
     - Initialize transaction: /initialize
     - Verify transaction: /verify
     - List transactions: /transaction

3. CLOUDINARY (Media Storage)
   - Service: Cloudinary
   - Used for: User avatars, shipment photos, documentation images
   - Keys needed:
     * CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME
     * CLOUDINARY_API_KEY
     * CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET
   - Documentation: https://cloudinary.com/documentation
   - Use case: Image upload, transformation, storage

4. SMTP / EMAIL (Nodemailer)
   - Service: Any SMTP email server
   - Used for: User registration, password reset, shipment notifications
   - Variables needed:
     * SMTP_HOST (e.g., smtp.gmail.com, smtp.mailtrap.io)
     * SMTP_PORT (e.g., 587 for TLS, 465 for SSL)
     * SMTP_USER (email username)
     * SMTP_PASS (email password or app password)
   - Documentation: https://nodemailer.com/about/

5. GOOGLE MAPS (Geolocation)
   - Service: Google Cloud Maps Platform
   - Used for: Rider location tracking, customer delivery addresses, route planning
   - Variable: GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY
   - Documentation: https://developers.google.com/maps
   - Required APIs:
     - Maps JavaScript API
     - Geocoding API
     - Directions API (optional)

6. REDIS (Caching/Queues)
   - Service: Redis (or Redis-compatible)
   - Used for: Real-time tracking, session caching, job queues
   - Variable: REDIS_URL
   - Documentation: https://redis.io/docs/

7. JWT (Authentication)
   - Used for: Access token and refresh token generation
   - Variables:
     * JWT_SECRET - Sign access tokens
     * JWT_REFRESH_SECRET - Sign refresh tokens
   - Library: jsonwebtoken (Node.js)

--- FRONTEND CONFIGURATION ---

8. VITE_API_URL
   - Used by: Vite build process
   - Purpose: Configures API base URL for frontend environment
   - Value example: https://kanoconnect-api.onrender.com
   - Definition: vite.env.ts or .env file at build time

--- BACKEND CONFIGURATION ---

9. NODE_ENV
   - Value: production
   - Purpose: Sets Node.js environment mode

10. PORT
    - Value: 10000
    - Purpose: Server listening port (Render sets this automatically)

11. CLIENT_URL
    - Purpose: Frontend URL for API CORS and redirect URIs
    - Value example: http://localhost:5173 (dev) or https://kano-web.onrender.com (prod)

--- RENDER DEPLOYMENT ---

render.yaml Configuration:
- Service 1: kanoconnect-api (Node.js backend)
  - Build: cd backend && npm install
  - Start: cd backend && npm start
  - Health check: /health
  - Runtime: node

- Service 2: kanoconnect (Static frontend)
  - Build: cd frontend && npm install && npm run build
  - Publish: frontend/dist
  - Runtime: static

--- SECURITY NOTES ---

- All environment variables marked with sync: false must be set manually in Render Dashboard
- Never commit .env files or sensitive values to the repository
- Use Render's "Environment" section to add each variable per service
- Recommended: Use Render's secret management for JWT secrets, Paystack keys, etc.

--- END OF DOCUMENT ---